ets price Luria around 90% to win", "Even fundraising and a favorable national environment offset Kiggans's incumbency"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Democratic-leaning environment in an even-PVI district, and the consensus of ten raters tilts clearly toward a Luria flip. The single recent poll shows a modest 3-point Luria lead, and markets price her near 90%, so a Lean D forecast with a mid-single-digit Democratic margin fits the evidence.", "watch": "Any new independent or Republican-sponsored polling showing Kiggans tied or ahead would move this back toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jen Kiggans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 2nd District is a rematch between incumbent Republican Jen Kiggans and former Democratic Representative Elaine Luria in an even-partisanship Hampton Roads seat. Fundraising is essentially even, with both candidates near $7.3 million raised and comparable cash on hand, so money is not a differentiator.\n\nThe evidence tilts Democratic. A Christopher Newport University poll in mid-October showed Luria leading by 3 points among likely voters, and most expert raters call the race Lean D or Likely D for a flip, with only two calling it a Tossup. Prediction markets price Luria's chances around 90 percent. The national midterm environment appears favorable to Democrats, and veterans-focused messaging is a theme in the race. Kiggans's incumbency is her main structural advantage, but it is not enough to offset the rest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7963, "margin": 4.98}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8168, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.777, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7659, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.762, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7557, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.771, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7851, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p